Welcome to Speaking of Psychology, a podcast from the American Psychological Association. I'm your host, Caitlin Luna. I'm joined by two guests. We have Dr. Lynn Buffka, Associate Executive Director for Research and Policy at APA and an APA fellow. And we have Dr. Jeannie Safer, an APA fellow who has been in private practice for over 40 years. She's also the host of the podcast. I love you, but I hate your politics. Our discussion is on managing stress at holiday gatherings during these divisive times.
欢迎收听《心理学谈话》（Speaking of Psychology），这是美国心理学协会（APA）出品的一档播客。我是主持人凯特琳·卢纳（Caitlin Luna）。今天和我一起参加节目录制的有两位嘉宾。一位是琳恩·巴夫卡博士（Dr. Lynn Buffka），她是APA负责研究与政策的副执行主任，也是APA资深会员。另一位是吉尼·赛弗博士（Dr. Jeannie Safer），她是一位APA资深会员，从事私人心理诊疗已有40多年。她也是播客《我爱你，但我讨厌你的政治立场》（I love you, but I hate your politics）的主播。我们今天的讨论主题是：在当今这个意见分歧的时代，如何在节日聚会中管理压力。

2
00:00:47.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Welcome, Dr. Buffka and Dr. Safer. Glad to be here. Thanks for having us. So at this point, we've made it past Thanksgiving and Hanukkah, and now Christmas and New Year's are upon us, and for many work holiday parties. So there's no doubt in my mind that people out there have experienced at least one uncomfortable conversation with a loved one or a friend. So we're looking for advice today on how to navigate these very tricky topics.
欢迎巴夫卡博士和赛弗博士。很高兴来到这里。谢谢你们邀请我们。目前，我们已经度过了感恩节和光明节，圣诞节和新年马上就要到了，对许多人来说，还有公司的节日派对。因此，我毫不怀疑，大家在现实生活中都已经和亲人或朋友经历过至少一次尴尬的对话。所以今天我们想寻求一些建议，告诉我们该如何应对这些非常棘手的话题。

3
00:01:12.000 --> 00:02:03.000
with people we care about. So I'll start with you, Dr. Safer. What advice do you have? Well, the first thing is that everybody's nervous. It's not just you. That's why every magazine, every internet thing, has 5,000 articles on other things to talk about at the holidays, except politics. There was a thing in the New York Times about this. There was something on Huffington. Isn't it sad that we can't think of anything to talk about other than politics these days? I find that very distressing. And one of the things that I recommend to people is that you could change the subject. I give you permission. Everybody will be happy if you do. Don't rise to the bait because some people can't get off their hobby horse, but you don't have to be on there with them. And, Lynn, what advice do you have?
与我们在乎的人交流。所以我先问您，赛弗博士。您有什么建议？嗯，首先的一点是，每个人都很紧张。不只是你。这就是为什么每本杂志、每一个网络平台上都有5000篇关于节日期间除了政治之外还能聊点什么的各类文章。《纽约时报》上曾刊登过相关内容，赫芬顿邮报上也有。现在的状况难道不是很悲哀吗？除了政治，我们竟然想不出任何其他可以谈论的话题。我觉得这非常苦恼。我向大家推荐的方法之一就是，你可以转换话题。我赋予你们这个权利。如果你这么做了，大家都会很高兴。不要去咬钩，因为有些人就是戒不掉他们的老毛病，但你没必要和他们陷在一起。那么，琳恩，你有什么建议呢？

