know what you're doing and you have a plan because otherwise it always gets into terrible territory, I think. I really recommend we not do it at not at a gathering. Absolutely. Because most people, if you have a very strong difference of opinion on, you're not changing their mind at a holiday gathering. You're not changing their mind at all. And that's that's one of the points of, of my podcast and of my upcoming book with the same name. Don't go into a conversation thinking you're going to change somebody's mind because first of all, minds are very difficult to change and you're not going to accomplish it. If they do it, it's because they want to change their mind. So once you get out of the idea of trying to change somebody's mind, it opens your horizons to have a conversation.
知道自己在做什么，并且有一个计划，否则我认为它总是会演变成糟糕的境地。我强烈建议我们不要这么做，不要在聚会上这么做。绝对是的。因为对于绝大多数人来说，如果你在某个问题上有非常强烈的意见分歧，你在节日聚会上是无法改变他们的看法的。你根本不可能改变他们的想法。这也是我的播客以及我即将出版的同名书籍的核心观点之一。不要抱着“我要改变别人的想法”这种念头去开始一段对话，因为首先，人的想法是非常难以改变的，你是绝对做不到的。如果他们改变了，那也是因为他们自己想要改变。所以，一旦你抛弃了试图改变别人想法的想法，你的视野就会开阔，从而能够进行真正的对话。

